I don't want to make a flame war our of this, but...
 
I don't think this is good advice to be giving newbies.  The
protection racket is in my mind an advanced tactic.  I mean, this guy
is NEW.  He needs to learn about stuff like praying, IDing wands
through engrave, altars, Elbereth, etc.
 
Dan, here's a couple easy tips that you might not have thought about:
 
- Never attack nymphs in the early game... just let them sleep
- If you find an altar, you can drop things on it to find out if
they're blessed, uncursed, or cursed.  You can also #offer fresh
monster corpses on it.
- If you find a wand, you can engrave with it and it might give you a
clue as to what it does.  e.g. if you get "The bugs on the floor slow
down!" then it's a wand of slow monster.
- When you're low on HP, or if you're starving and have no food, try
using #pray.  Your god usually fixes problems for you if you pray. 
However, you don't want to pray TOO often, otherwise your god gets
angry at you, so only save it for emergencies.

